; Lead: BrokkAi/bifrost-packs#192 (CVE-2024-34156), version-independent part.
; Product source contract: the encoding/gob package documentation says the
; decoder is not hardened against adversarial input, and CVE-2024-34156 shows a
; crafted stream exhausting the stack. Fixed toolchains still decode untrusted
; streams with that documented limit, so connection bytes reaching
; gob.NewDecoder are reported on every Go toolchain. The CVE's affected-version
; part needs toolchain evidence the engine does not have
; (research/go-rust-cve/README.md).
; Engine contract: sources and the sink bind exactly to the reviewed
; bifrost.go.stdlib.net and bifrost.go.stdlib.encoding-gob models. Calls through
; net.Conn and net.Listener close only through those models' summaries that
; claim covers_overrides. Any other call on the path must be modeled, so an
; unmodeled wrapper such as bufio.NewReader leaves the run inconclusive instead
; of clean.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.security.go.gob-decode-network-input"
  :name "Go network connection decoded with encoding/gob"
  :message "bytes from a network connection reach gob.NewDecoder"
  :severity warning
  :description "Reports net.Dial, net.DialTimeout and net.Listener.Accept connections that reach the reader operand of encoding/gob.NewDecoder. The gob decoder is documented as not hardened against adversarial input (CVE-2024-34156), so a peer controls a decoder that can exhaust resources on any toolchain."
  :tags ["security" "go" "deserialization" "cwe-502"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type taint
      :mode may
      :call-modeling (call-modeling :unmodeled require-model)
      :sources
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (source
              :id net-dial
              :display-name "net.Dial connection"
              :categories [io.external]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (resolved-call
                      :resolves-to "net.Dial"
                      :proof declared
                      (call-bindings
                        (call-shape
                          (call :callee (name "Dial") :arity 2))))))
              :bind (result :index 0)
              :labels [untrusted])
            (source
              :id net-dial-timeout
              :display-name "net.DialTimeout connection"
              :categories [io.external]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (resolved-call
                      :resolves-to "net.DialTimeout"
                      :proof declared
                      (call-bindings
                        (call-shape
                          (call :callee (name "DialTimeout") :arity 3))))))
              :bind (result :index 0)
              :labels [untrusted])
            (source
              :id net-listener-accept
              :display-name "net.Listener.Accept connection"
              :categories [io.external]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (resolved-call
                      :resolves-to "net.Listener.Accept"
                      :proof declared
                      (call-bindings
                        (call-shape
                          (call :callee (name "Accept") :arity 0))))))
              :bind (result :index 0)
              :labels [untrusted])])
      :sinks
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (sink
              :id gob-new-decoder-reader
              :display-name "gob.NewDecoder reader"
              :categories [deserialization]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (call-argument :formal-index 0
                      (resolved-call
                        :resolves-to "encoding/gob.NewDecoder"
                        :proof declared
                        (call-bindings
                          (call-shape
                            (call :callee (name "NewDecoder") :arity 1)))))))
              :dangerous-operand (argument :index 0)
              :accepts [untrusted])]))
  :classification
    (classification
      :fallback (classification-id :taxonomy "CWE" :id "502")))
